  "about": "Scripted Claude Code sessions in project/ for scripts/eval-tagger.py. Each scenario's last turn is judged. 'expect' gives the right words for that turn: a list of acceptable values, null meaning the key should be left out; for the 'missing' list key, '~a|b' means not 'none' and naming at least one of a, b. A key not in 'expect' isn't scored. 'skill': 'auto' is worked out from the session: helped or unneeded when a skill ran, else none, would-help or left out. Scenarios with \"set\": \"holdout\" were written after the judge's instructions were tuned on the rest, and never used to tune them: they show how the tuning holds up on work it hasn't seen.",
